message: >-
  If you use Termyte in academic work, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
title: "Termyte"
abstract: >-
  Termyte is a local-first memory layer for AI coding agents. It captures
  every tool call, file read, file write, shell command, and final response
  from a coding agent (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Cursor, Gemini CLI,
  Windsurf, and any MCP-compatible client), stores them in a local SQLite
  database, and synthesizes them into searchable, durable memories. The next
  time the agent opens the project, Termyte surfaces the relevant memories
  as context — so the agent does not have to rediscover what you already
  know.
date-released: 2026-06-28
